{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeeyUydk5rcZcm11LC1C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the three candidate files and the check command printed `OK`. On its short test fit (100 draws, one chain) the model scored ELPD-LOO −1047.8; the incumbent's full fit scores −1069.9. That gap is only a hint, because the short fit isn't a full fit.\n\n**What I refined:** the incumbent, `length_scaled_alternation_ideal`. The name is `person_sensitivity_length_scaled_ideal`.\n\n**The one change:** in the incumbent, everyone shares one sensitivity to how far a sequence's switch rate is from their personal ideal. Here each person gets their own sensitivity, drawn from a population distribution. Some people almost always pick the sequence nearer their ideal; others lean toward it only weakly. Everything else is kept: the personal ideal switch rate, the scaling by sequence length and the shared penalty for repeating patterns. The person-level slots have room for new participants (400 of them), so the next experiment's design can still use this model.\n\n**Why this change:** the tied rival `personal_ideal_with_personal_lapse` suggests people differ in how consistently they act on their impression, and the incumbent has nothing for that. The critique pointed at long streaks instead, but that result doesn't survive the false-discovery correction (q = 0.144). I also didn't take the streak route: one streak-penalty model has already lost to the best, and another adds nothing measurable over the model it refines.\n\n**What the check didn't cover:**\n- **Novelty:** a per-person sensitivity changes the predictions for the population, but I can't confirm they clear the novelty gate's threshold against the incumbent.\n- **Convergence:** a one-chain run can't report R-hat. The full admission fit still has to pass the divergence, R-hat and effective-sample-size limits, and finish within 30 minutes.\n- **Reliability warning:** on the short fit, 8.6% of trials had high Pareto-k values (the tolerance is 1%). A per-person parameter often does this, so the full fit's ELPD may be flagged as unreliable.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_4/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2897,"cache_read_input_tokens":64546,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2897,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9007b96c-b538-4e84-a6c4-a937edd124eb","uuid":"07dced07-15df-46a6-9f84-64ca26ce6fd4","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:15:31.484Z","request_id":"req_011CfeeyUbobUG1g93mLsVW2"}
